  Creative moves:
    - Detected the MG5 param card failure by noticing the LO cross section (0.9045 pb) was far too high for 550 GeV sparticles, then traced it to MG5 ignoring the SLHA and using default masses. Fixed by copying the restrict_default.dat template and modifying masses in-place.
    - When pyhepmc from_hepevt segfaulted on events with ~1800 particles, the agent wrote a minimal pythia_to_hepmc_simple function that constructs GenEvents with only beam (status 4) and final-state (status 1) particles, sufficient for Delphes input.

  Stuck points:
