    - Initial MG5 param card approach used 'set param_card' commands which were silently ignored, leading to generation with wrong masses. Required a full re-generation of 50k events.

  Issues:
    - The Z mass window was set to 86-96 GeV (±5 GeV around m_Z) instead of the standard CMS on-Z selection of |m_ℓℓ - m_Z| < 15 GeV (76.2-106.2 GeV). This narrower window loses Z→ℓℓ events in the Breit-Wigner tails and detector-smeared tails, likely accounting for a significant fraction of the ~40% yield deficit relative to the reference.
    - The analysis uses NLO (Prospino 2.1) rather than NLO+NLL cross sections used by CMS. The report acknowledges this as a ~5% effect. Additionally, the Delphes fast-sim with no pileup systematically differs from the CMS full simulation, contributing to the overall ~40% deficit.

